{"path":"utility/functional/reference_wrapper/reference_wrapper","title":"std::reference_wrapper<T>::reference_wrapper","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::reference_wrapper&lt;T&gt;::</span>reference_wrapper","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/reference_wrapper/reference_wrapper","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Constructs a new reference wrapper.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>reference_wrapper<span class=\"br0\">(</span> U<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> x <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*see below*/</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(constexpr since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">reference_wrapper<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> reference_wrapper<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(constexpr since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Constructs a new reference wrapper.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Converts <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> to <code>T&amp;</code> as if by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> t <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>, then stores a reference to <code>t</code>. This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/decay\"><span class=\"kw633\">std::<span class=\"me2\">decay</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">type</span></span></code> is not the same type as <code>reference_wrapper</code> and the expression <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">FUN<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/declval\"><span class=\"kw1128\">std::<span class=\"me2\">declval</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is well-formed, where <code>FUN</code> names the set of imaginary functions\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> FUN<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> FUN<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> delete<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Copy constructor. Stores a reference to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> an object to wrap\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> another reference wrapper\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <div class=\"t-noexcept-full\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;\n<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>FUN<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/declval\"><span class=\"kw1128\">std::<span class=\"me2\">declval</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></span></div></div> where <code>FUN</code> is the set of imaginary functions described in the description above.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2993\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2993</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td>deleted <code>reference_wrapper(T&amp;&amp;)</code> constructor interferes<br> with overload resolution in some cases\n</td>\n<td>replaced with a constructor template\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/functional","title":"Function objects"},{"path":"utility/functional/reference_wrapper","title":"std::reference_wrapper"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::reference_wrapper<T>::reference_wrapper","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Constructs a new reference wrapper."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"x, other"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"noexcept specification: noexcept(noexcept(FUN(std::declval<U>()))) where FUN is the set of imaginary functions described in the description above."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":175,"codeBlockCount":1}
